+## Genuinely new mechanism and new connection
+
+### New mechanism: terminal-orbit Euler–Kummer coverage checksum
+
+History status: NEW_COMPOSITION relative to the complete frozen canonical history; not claimed literature-new. The ingredients are promoted separately, but their executable composition was not recorded.
+
+For a normalized exact pair and squarefree generic fibre, L3/L4/L5-exact supplies terminal records
+
+~~~text
+(h, chart, kappa, strict truncation F),  deg p_(h,F)=1,
+e_S = kappa / gcd(kappa, supp F),
+complete leaf orbit <-> normalized boundary place.
+~~~
+
+Independently, the marked finite-end theorem gives
+
+~~~text
+sum over finite ends S of e_S = td + b1(C) - 1.
+~~~
+
+Compose them as a coverage checksum: classify each certified terminal physical place as finite or pole using the other-coordinate valuation; deduplicate by the certified deck orbit; rescale cover orders by kappa/e_S; and compare the sum with an independently computed td+b1(C)-1. Delete-one-orbit and duplicate-one-orbit mutations are mandatory.
+
+A pass certifies only terminal inventory completeness for that exact pair/fibre. It does not prove a book landing, occurrence, or target-component grouping. A failure exposes a missing/duplicated place, wrong cover/place scaling, or source defect. Only after a pass should one attempt to continue terminal records in the fibre parameter and eliminate their finite limits into component-labelled A(F) factors. If those labels are not canonical, return OPEN; never infer a target meridian from a cv flag or equal special-fibre values.
+
+This connects Avenue 2's intrinsic exact-pair terminals to Avenue 7's missing component-labelled asymptotic curve and Avenue 25's marked finite-end filter. It is not the stopped TDIC test: the latter lacked precisely the terminal inventory and target-component custody that this mechanism tries to construct.
